            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sleep researchers recommend that adults get seven to nine hours of sleep per night. However, surveys in several countries show that many adults sleep less than seven hours on weekdays. Some studies link short sleep to weight gain, although the exact reasons are still being investigated. Napping for 20 minutes during the day can improve alertness, but longer naps may make people feel groggy.",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
